// control-h0-nodepth twin (t_96daf53b): sd_h0_nodepth.fcg with the ONE token
// changed - out float4 instead of out half4.  Its container clears
// outputFromH0 and its last instruction writes the full-precision output
// register where the H0 side writes the half one, so the SDK builds a
// different control word for it (the values and their provenance live in
// cell/gcm/gcm_fp_control.h, not here).  That is what makes the pair an
// experiment on the bind rather than on the compiler: both sides are
// reference-compiled, and this side is the expectation the other is judged
// against - the vertex program's own Z on every pixel.
void main(float4 t : TEXCOORD0, out float4 o : COLOR)
{
    o = t;
}
